Pages 1 and 2 have an extra empty text item `""` at y=9 with height 0 → counts as content (doesn't contain "| Page") → false failure.

So my check should ignore empty strings. Fix verify script: filter out items with `str.trim() === ""` when computing content items (and also when building pageTexts it's harmless).

Also improve the overlap check to be zone-based:
- footer items: those containing `Page ${p} of`
- content items: non-empty items not containing footer
- assert min content y >= 26 (band top) — this is the meaningful check; plus footer y < 26.

Let me update the check to:
```ts
const BAND = 26;
const footerItems = items.filter(i => /Page \d+ of \d+/.test(i.str));
const contentItems = items.filter(i => i.str.trim() !== "" && !/Page \d+ of \d+/.test(i.str));
const footerInBand = footerItems.every(i => i.y < BAND) && footerItems.length > 0;
const contentOutOfBand = contentItems.every(i => i.y - Math.max(i.height,0)*0.5 >= BAND - 0.5);
```
Hmm, for content: baseline y of the lowest text should be >= BAND (26) on doc pages; on cover/index >= 40 ✓. So `contentItems.every(i => i.y >= BAND - 1)`.

Let's apply.

input.newString:
let overlap = false;
const overlapPages: number[] = [];
const BAND = 26; // reserved footer band height in points
const footerRe = /Page \d+ of \d+/;
for (let p = 1; p <= totalPages; p++) {
  const items = pageItems[p - 1];
  const footerItems = items.filter((i) => footerRe.test(i.str));
  const contentItems = items.filter(
    (i) => i.str.trim() !== "" && !footerRe.test(i.str)
  );
  const footerInsideBand =
    footerItems.length > 0 && footerItems.every((i) => i.y < BAND);
  const contentOutsideBand = contentItems.every((i) => i.y >= BAND - 1);
  if (!footerInsideBand || !contentOutsideBand) {
    overlap = true;
    overlapPages.push(p);
  }
}
check(
  "footer: sits in its own reserved band (no overlap)",
  !overlap,
  overlapPages.length ? `pages ${overlapPages.join(", ")}` : undefined
);

